WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.440
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: build a small Task Tracker end to end. Combine variables, decisions, loops, and functions. Ship something you can show on a portfolio.

2
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:27.706
Design before you code: Design before you code. List features like add, list, complete, and quit. Decide how tasks are stored. Sketch the menu loop on paper first.

3
00:00:28.556 --> 00:00:39.764
Core loop pattern: Use a core loop pattern. Show a menu. Read the user’s choice. Run the matching action, then show the menu again.

4
00:00:40.614 --> 00:00:54.342
Make it robust: Make it robust. Handle empty input and bad menu choices. Confirm before deleting if you add delete. Keep messages clear for beginners testing your app.

5
00:00:55.192 --> 00:01:07.168
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: building every feature before the menu works. No way to quit the loop. Mixing storage format so list and complete disagree.

6
00:01:08.018 --> 00:01:20.618
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: get add and list working first. Then add complete and quit. Then continue in the written Module 7 project and acceptance checks.
